# Chapter 01 — Company Profile

## Meridian Community Bank at a Glance

| | |
|---|---|
| **Founded** | 1998 |
| **HQ** | Charlotte, NC (Myers Park branch + administrative offices) |
| **Second location** | Manhattan, NY (financial district retail branch) |
| **Employees** | 118 |
| **Total assets** | ~$480 million |
| **Charter** | North Carolina state-chartered, FDIC insured |
| **Regulator** | NC Office of the Commissioner of Banks + FDIC; NY DFS 
  (via NY branch) |

Meridian is a community bank in the classic mold: locally focused, 
relationship-driven lending, and retail deposits. It was founded to serve 
small businesses and homeowners in the Charlotte area. The Manhattan branch 
was opened in 2018 to serve commercial clients and transplants with North 
Carolina ties, and it brought Meridian under NY DFS jurisdiction — a 
compliance wrinkle the bank is still adapting to.

